From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: require coordinated reset on Uke

Uke must not fall back to an uncoordinated GPIO pulse if its reset phandle
is missing. Reject that description before requesting a GPIO or enabling
any supply. The existing USBSS child owns reset timing and protection.
Other boards retain the legacy GPIO path.

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -3270,6 +3270,10 @@ static int wcd939x_populate_dt_data(struct wcd939x_priv *wcd939x, struct device *dev)
 #endif /* CONFIG_TYPEC */
 	int ret;
 
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,uke") &&
+	    !of_property_present(dev->of_node, "resets"))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL, "Uke requires coordinated codec reset\n");
+
 	if (of_property_present(dev->of_node, "resets")) {
 		if (of_property_present(dev->of_node, "reset-gpios"))
 			return -EINVAL;
